<worksheet>
    <title>Representing Linear Functions Task</title>
    <objectives>
        <ul>
            <li>
                <p>
                    Understanding linear functions
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>
                    Being able to represent linear functions in multiple ways
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>
                    Finding connections
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>
                    Communicating using words, pictures, diagrams, colors, etc.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>
                    Performing basic computations
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>Crafting explanations
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>
                    Writing and revising for clarity and precision
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>
                    Planning the layout of the final product

                </p>
            </li>
            <li>Deciding on the important information to include (or not)
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>
                    Putting strategies into words
                </p>
            </li>
        </ul>
    </objectives>
    <task>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Task:As a group, show four different ways to solve the following prompt.  At least one strategy must be visual.  Clearly show connections across strategies.
            </p>
            <p>
                Ben was recently looking at the possibility of joining a gym.  He called around to different gyms and the gym closest to his house had an initial membership fee of $50 and then a monthly fee of $36 per month.  How many months can he keep the membership if he has $600?

            </p>
        </statement>
    </task>
    <task>
        <statement>
            <p>
                Create a final product to turn in that contains:
            </p>
        
        <ul>
            <li>
                <p>
                    Show each strategy that you used to solve the prompt.  You can use grids, pictures, charts, words, or any other tools you need to make your explanation clear and easy to understand.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>
                    Show connections across strategies.
                </p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>
                    Include work from each person using their color.
                </p>
            </li>
        </ul>
        </statement>
    </task>

</worksheet>
    
    